<main id="source-and-status" tabindex="-1" class="page-width article-body">
<header class="product-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Source &amp; status</p><h1>Inspect what exists.<br>Know its scope.</h1><p class="article-deck">The site explains the Lab model and provides a selected source edition. The local operational foundation and the products being developed around it have different scopes.</p></header>
<section id="available" aria-labelledby="available-title"><h2 id="available-title">What exists today</h2>
<p>The local Lab foundation records governed work and supports reconstruction of project knowledge. The <a href="governance-lab-reference.html#today">operational-scope chapter</a> identifies its accepted foundation, proposed updates and outstanding release work.</p>
<p>This website is a static documentation edition. A stable installable Lab release, hosted service, automatic ontology coverage and operational Craft connector have not been established by this edition.</p>
<p>Craft is a separate software-design product under development for closed beta. Its <a href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html#craft-overview">article</a> explains the selected modeling and compiler scope.</p></section>
<section id="inspect" aria-labelledby="inspect-title"><h2 id="inspect-title">Inspect the selected source</h2>
<p>The linked Lab records and implementations were captured on 8 October 2026. They are an inspectable source selection, with recorded identities and fingerprints. They do not automatically track later repository changes.</p>
<ul><li><a href="lab-reference-library.html#reference">Definitions, record formats and connection contracts</a></li><li><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/v1/README.md">Local runtime usage and implementation scope</a></li><li><a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/v1/lab_runtime/governance.py">Governance resolver implementation</a></li><li><a href="lab-reference-library.html#research">Research sources and open questions</a></li></ul>
<p>An exact record's own standing determines whether its meaning governs the work. Inclusion in this website supplies a reading route, without granting admission or operational permission.</p></section>
<section id="contribute" aria-labelledby="contribute-title"><h2 id="contribute-title">Review and contribute</h2>
<p>For a documentation correction, identify the page and passage, explain the problem and include a concrete replacement or supporting source. Keep changes to accepted definitions on their declared review and admission route.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/cyberAlchemyAI/CyberAlchemy-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the development repository</a> to inspect the current tree and use its available contribution routes. The captured source links above provide the selected documentation edition here.</p>
<p><a href="prepare-definition.html">Prepare a proposed definition</a> or <a href="research/reader-study.html">send a downloaded reading-study response to the person who shared the site</a>.</p></section>
</main>{{FOOTER}}</body></html>
